{
 "note": "Kyst restaurant and Jetty Bar, with the Sandbox takeaway at its north-east end, in one publicly owned leasehold building on the Busselton foreshore west of the jetty (1 Foreshore Parade; the old Equinox cafe, rebuilt in 2015, Kyst since about 2022). From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) and an OpenTable photo. A spread of pale grey weatherboard wings under white Colorbond roofs covered in solar panels: a hipped west wing (the restaurant) with two gables pushing out to the south, a low hipped middle, a tall east wing whose ridge runs to the beach, and two gables at the south-east tip. Gable ends have white barges and dark bronze-framed glass up into the apex. The front here is the south-south-west side, towards Foreshore Parade, which is what drivers see; big figs and pines stand round it. Names are plain lettering, no logos. Metres: x left to right as seen from the south (bearing 115), y back towards the beach (bearing 25).",
